course: dictionary
lesson: 3308
title: Words from the ancient world
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name people, places or things from long ago. Etruscan is one of them. When you meet a word you do not know, look for clues in the sentence. «The Etruscan tombs in the museum had painted walls.» Tombs are where the dead are buried, and museums show old things, so Etruscan must describe something from a very old time.
explain: Etruscan can work in three ways: as an adjective, as a word for the people, and as the name of their language. «Etruscan kings» and «the Etruscan alphabet» describe things. «The Etruscans» means the people themselves. Ask yourself: is the word describing something, or naming someone? Your answer tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Context can also show you where a word belongs. «The Romans took the alphabet from the Greeks and the Etruscans» tells you the Etruscans were a people close to Rome, and that they helped shape the letters we use today. You do not need every detail to see that Etruscan belongs to history.
fact: Etruscan means belonging to the Etruscans, their art or their language.
fact: The Etruscans were an ancient people who lived in central Italy, in an area called Etruria, before and during the early days of Rome.
fact: «Etruscan» is also the name of their language, which used an alphabet like the Greek one.
fact: The Etruscan language is still only partly understood by experts today.
fact: The Etruscans came up in Rome's history as neighbours who ruled Rome for a time and taught the Romans things such as arches.
exercise: «The Etruscan alphabet looked a bit like the Greek one.» What does Etruscan mean here? | *Belonging to the Etruscans, their letters | A kind of Greek food | A brand-new modern invention | A type of bird
exercise: Which word in «The Etruscans lived in central Italy long ago» names a people? | Lived | Italy | *Etruscans | Central
exercise: «The Etruscan shrew is one of the smallest mammals.» What is an Etruscan shrew? | *A tiny animal, one of the smallest mammals | A huge ship from Rome | A painted tomb in a museum | A kind of Greek bread
test: «Etruscan tombs» in museums are famous for what? | Wooden ships only | Fast cars | *Painted tombs and bronze statues | Snow and ice
test: In «Etruscan is also the name of their language», what does Etruscan name? | A modern language everyone speaks fluently | *The language of the Etruscans, still only partly understood | A kind of alphabet used only by the Romans | A city in Italy that is still busy today
exam: Which sentence uses Etruscan as a word for a people? | «Etruscan kings once ruled Rome for a time» | «Etruscan tombs are full of paintings» | *«The Etruscans were neighbours of early Rome» | «The Etruscan alphabet was like the Greek one»
